<text textLength="286" lengthAdjust="spacing"><textPath href="#bdg" textLength="286" lengthAdjust="spacing">Hablamos espa&#241;ol &#183; English &#183;</textPath></text></svg><span>ES</span></div></section><section class="sec"><div class="wrap split top post-grid"><div class="prose reveal"><h2>Pavers and ballast on flat roofs</h2>
<p>Jemza Roofing does paver and ballasted roof work in Salt Lake City. Our photos show a grid of pavers turning a flat roof into a usable deck, and gravel ballast on a lower flat roof next to a shingle roof.</p>
<p>On a ballasted roof, the weight of loose stone or pavers holds the roof membrane in place instead of fasteners or glue. Pavers also make a walking surface, which is why they&rsquo;re used for rooftop decks.</p>
<h3>Flat roofs with a view</h3>
<p>Rooftop decks often share the roof with a chimney. The long black shroud in the photo below sits right beside a paver deck; see more in <a href="ChimneyCap-Shroud.php">chimney caps &amp; shrouds</a>.</p></div>
